codemap 9
tour platform-loop
kind flow
author ai
group render
note The window and the event loop, in the platform crate, and the only place this program blocks. winit owns the loop; the application is one trait, App, built around one method, frame (the other two answer a test script), so nothing above here knows what a window event is - the gui crate sees ui's Input going in and a Frame with a DrawList coming out. The loop is not a game loop: it waits for events and redraws only when input arrived or a deadline the last frame asked for came due, so an idle codemap costs one frame a second. Every event does the same two things - update the accumulated Input and mark a redraw pending - and the redraw turns that Input into one frame, has the Renderer present it, and clears the momentary part. Under CODEMAP_SCRIPT or CODEMAP_SHOT the window is fixed at 1600x1000 and scale 1 and ignores the real mouse and keyboard, so a scripted run looks the same on every machine; the script itself is the platform-script flow.

