note The whole interface between the loop and the application: frame, given the Renderer (as the Measure and for scale and screenshots) and the frame's input, returning a Frame; script and locate answer the lines of a test script the loop does not understand itself and the element names it aims at. script returning Retry means the line is not done and runs again next frame; locate says whether the named element was visible last frame and where its centre was. This is why the gui crate never mentions winit.

